# Go sources are compiled as bytes, and the build id covers them: a checkout
# whose .go files carry CRLF produces a different binary from one whose files
# carry LF. Pinning them to LF makes `go build -trimpath -buildvcs=false`
# reproduce the released binaries on any platform, which is a claim the release
# notes make and a reviewer will check.
#
# Only the compiled files need this. Prose files are read by people, and the
# module files are parsed rather than hashed into the build id — a CRLF go.mod
# was measured to make no difference.
*.go text eol=lf
